  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe machined mesh in the viewer's stock slot (M13.1) now shows two things it did not before:\n\n- **Deviation classes on the mesh.** Each facet is judged once per mesh, using the same rule the GPU eye uses: the model's `DistanceLattice` (`pack_target`) is read at the facet centroid, with the gate `gate_tol(DEV_TOL, view cell)`. The result is one of four classes: clean, rest, gouge or unjudged. The code is in the new `app::machined_classes` module. The classes are cached in `stock_export::MeshCache` (`classify` / `viewed_classes`) and computed in `ui::machined::prime` alongside the extraction. `world::collect_parts` expands them into the stock part's per-vertex class buffer, so the mesh uses the sheet's and the eye's legend colours. Nothing is computed per frame, and the STL export path does not pay for the classes.\n- **Hovered facet highlight.** When the mesh answers a stock hover, `machined::filter_hit_facet` returns the triangle the ray hit. It is stored in `State::hover_mesh`, which is view state, not a command, and is cleared on every hover refresh. The shell draws it as a yellow translucent fill with an outline in the hover colour, projected through the camera each frame, so moving the pointer causes no GPU re-upload. If no mesh stands, or a corner projects behind the camera, nothing is drawn.\n\nThe extractor is unchanged. The sim crate is untouched, apart from public items it already exported.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/25-mesh-hover-deviation.md`.\n\n## Results\n\n- Faced fixture (12x12x20 box faced to z 18 over a 12x12x18 model): every up-facing facet on the faced top classifies clean. The class buffer has the same length as the vertex buffer, and only the four class values appear.\n- A second `prime` reuses the same classes `Arc`, so nothing is judged twice.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `app::machined_classes::tests`: `the_boundaries_belong_to_clean`, `no_number_no_verdict` (NaN, infinite readings and a NaN tolerance give unjudged; nothing panics), `no_target_paints_every_facet_unjudged`, `facets_on_above_and_under_the_model_class_as_such`.\n- `ui::machined_tests`: `nothing_before_a_view_and_one_extraction_after` (now checks the classes, which were previously asserted to be empty), `the_hovered_mesh_facet_is_the_one_the_ray_hit_and_projects`.\n- `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick` fell back to the batch set, and every step passed: geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion and app suites, the ui suites run from `crates/ui`, and clippy with `-D warnings` (19.5 min). No snapshots changed.\n\nNot hand-tested in the GUI yet.\n\nChangelog: The machined stock mesh paints the Deviate classes (clean / rest / gouge / unjudged) and highlights the facet under the pointer.\n\nFixes #25\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
